messages:
kai (Frontend): Reporting a reproducible client LCP jump on /metrics/dashboard after this morning's canary. Heatmap and metric sparklines stall ~800-1200ms on first load. Not seen on prod-stable.

noa (Build): I ran a diff on the artifact bundles. The dashboard client bundle went from 2.0MB -> 4.7MB (gzipped). Suspect source-map concatenation + a new debug-utils import.

kai (Frontend): Flamegraph shows long parse + eval (~600ms) attributed to a ~1.9MB inline payload inside the bundle. Looks like an inlined vendor file (debug-utils) with a big license/source-map blob.

rin (Platform): We enabled the build pipeline plugin 'sourcemap-collector' in canary to centralize maps for debug. It accidentally switched from external source-map files to embedding them during the canary build. That would inflate gzipped size and push parse onto main.

noa (Build): Repro snippet from pipeline:
```
// build pipeline excerpt
plugins.push(new SourceMapCollector({ embed: true }));
// should be embed: false
```

kai (Frontend): If the source map bytes are embedded, Uglify + gzip still leaves a lot of bytes and the browser has to parse/eval that big chunk. Charts load after script parse -> chart init. So LCP suffers.

anya (SRE): Can we rollback the plugin config in the canary stream quickly? Canary is at 10% traffic. I'm already seeing client-lcp alert firing (avg 1.3s). If it hits 1.5s for 5m I'm going to flip the canary to stable.

rin (Platform): I'll flip the pipeline flag for the canary build to embed:false and trigger a rebuild. Also scanning rollout manifests for build-flags to ensure we didn't copy the change elsewhere.

noa (Build): Short-term mitigation: mark debug-utils as external so it doesn't get bundled into the chart chunk and re-enable separate .map files. Also tweak splitChunks to keep vendor libs out of the chart route:
```
optimization: {
  splitChunks: {
    cacheGroups: {
      vendors: { test: /[\\/]node_modules[\\/]/, name: 'vendors', chunks: 'all', priority: -10 },
      charts: { test: /charts-lib|debug-utils/, name: 'charts-vendor', chunks: 'async', priority: 10 }
    }
  }
}
```

kai (Frontend): Good call. One extra observation: the prefetch route logic is kicking in earlier now (rollout tweak that raised prefetch concurrency), so clients are fetching chart chunks aggressively during navigation and that amplifies the parse spike. We may want to lower prefetch concurrency for canary until bundle sizes are back to normal.

rin (Platform): I'll lower prefetch concurrency for canary from 6 -> 2 and add a perf gate in rollout controller: fail canary weight increase if median client-lcp delta > +200ms.

anya (SRE): Deploy-bot queued: eng-platform/canary rebuild @ 2026-01-11T09:22:10Z. If alerts persist after new build, I'll roll back to stable. :no_entry_sign:

kai (Frontend): After rebuild we'll run synthetic first-paint + heatmap render perf tests in CI and attach a sourcemap check that ensures maps are not embedded. Also adding a bundle-size regression alert to the console dashboard so future pipeline changes can't silently embed large blobs.

noa (Build): I'll open PR to revert the plugin default and add CI lint to block embed:true in production pipeline.

rin (Platform): TL;DR: canary pipeline mistakenly embedded sourcemaps and pulled debug-utils into chart chunk -> bundle bloat and parse/eval on main -> charts freeze. Immediate fixes: rebuild with embed:false, mark debug-utils external, reduce prefetch concurrency, add perf gate. Longer-term: rollout perf gate + build lint. :thumbsup:
